The grid parses cleanly. Structure: a diagonal stripe pattern fill(r,c) = (2*(r+c)+1) mod 10 in the interior, a 1-frame on rows 0-1 and cols 0-1, plus 4-markers along row 2 and column 2, with 126 zero cells (holes) to fill.

The main ambiguity: hole cells that fall on the frame (row 1) or on the 4-marker row (row 2) — should they be restored to 1/4, or filled with the pattern? A demo will settle this cheaply.

